<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tom Blount</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1739</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tom Blount (died 1739) was a chief of the northern Tuscarora towns in North Carolina in the early 18th century. Unlike Hancock's southern towns, his people stayed out of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuscarora-war">Tuscarora War</a> of 1711–1715 and made a separate peace with the colony, which recognised him as leader of the Tuscarora who remained. A reservation was later set aside for them on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roanoke-river">Roanoke River</a>.</p></div>
